{{wp|Hof|lang=de}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Hoff||in family names, otherwise obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|hof}}, from {{inh|de|goh|hof}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*hof}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hufą||hill, farm}}. See there for cognates.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/hoːf/|aa=standard}}
* {{IPA|de|/hɔf/|aa=northern and western Germany; becoming rare}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Hof.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{audio|de|De-Hof.ogg}}
* {{hyph|de|Hof}}
* {{rhymes|de|oːf|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m,(e)s,^e|dim=^chen}}

# [[yard]], [[court]], [[courtyard]] {{gloss|open area by a house or enclosed by houses}}
#: {{ux|de|Der '''Hof''' hinter unserm Haus ist mit Schiefer gepflastert.|The '''yard''' behind our house is paved with slate.}}
# [[court]] {{gloss|residence and entourage of a nobleman}}
#: {{ux|de|Am '''Hof''' des Königs gab es ständige Intrigen.|There were constant intrigues at the king's '''court'''.}}
# [[farmyard]] {{gloss|central area of a farm, excluding the fields}}
#: {{ux|de|Das Essen wird den Arbeitern ins Feld gebracht, damit sie erst abends auf den '''Hof''' zurückkommen müssen.|The workers are served food in the fields, so that they needn’t come back to the '''farmyard''' before the evening.}}
# {{lb|de|by extension}} [[farm]], [[agricultural]] [[enterprise]]
#: {{ux|de|Wenn mein Sohn den '''Hof''' nicht übernimmt, muss ich verkaufen.|If my son doesn’t take over the '''farm''', I’ll have to sell it.}}

